. The Rust `(v as usize) > len` mirrors this exactly. Also confirmed: `start == len` is valid (prints just `\\n`), `stop == start` is rejected, and the start check short-circuits both stop checks.\n\n## Suite is proven non-trivial\n\nSix mutations injected into `src/lib.rs` were each caught (3–12 case failures per mutation), then the baseline was restored and re-verified green:\n\nsigned-vs-unsigned start compare · signed-vs-unsigned stop compare · `<=` → `<` · `>` → `>=` off-by-one · diagnostic wording drift · default `stop = len-1`\n\n## Two notes\n\n- `translation/Cargo.toml`: added `libloading` to `[dev-dependencies]` as instructed, plus `harness = false` on the three test targets — the tests redirect fd 1 (process-global), and libtest's parallel progress lines were contaminating the captures. A sequential runner reporting on stderr fixed the 7 spurious failures this caused.\n- crates.io is blocked by the sandbox proxy; `libloading 0.8.9` was already in the local cargo cache, so all cargo commands use `--offline`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3054,"cache_read_input_tokens":107529,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3054,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0a8d044c-4e59-49f3-80ff-273b6d7f2594","uuid":"fddbb84a-c16c-427c-9908-af0fe831b197","timestamp":"2026-09-05T02:52:39.435Z"}
